      "type": "Classic Car Auction · ends 10 Dec",
      "description": "HIGHLIGHTS:\n• Registered with ASI and supplied with a certificate of historical significance\n• 1973 model with Bertone coachwork and a removable hardtop (Targa)\n• Engine modified to 1,500 cc and fitted with twin Weber carburettors\n• Fitted with RG Design alloy wheels, Made in Italy, and new tyres\n\nHISTORY/OVERVIEW:\nDesigned around Marcello Gandini’s futuristic styling for Carrozzeria Bertone and introduced in 1972, the Fiat X1/9 is one of the most iconic Italian mid-engined sports Targas. Its balanced weight distribution, pop-up headlights and removable hardtop, which stows in the front luggage compartment, combined distinctive styling with outstanding dynamic qualities. This 1973 example from the first series is registered with ASI and has been kept indoors over the years.\n\nBODYWORK/PAINT:\nThe bodywork is in good overall condition. It was restored and repainted in 1998 and has since been kept indoors. All exterior body parts are correct for the model. The seals, glass and removable hardtop are original to the period. The car is fitted with RG Design alloy wheels, Made in Italy, paired with new tyres.\n\nINTERIOR:\nThe cabin retains its original Bertone interior, which is free from damage. The only point to note is that the radio is missing from the dashboard.\n\nMECHANICAL:\nThe mechanical components include an engine with an indicated mileage of just 7,990 km from new. The original 1,300 cc displacement was later modified to 1,500 cc, with the addition of twin Weber carburettors. Since this mechanical work was carried out, the car has been used exclusively for classic car rallies. The seller states that the mechanical components are in excellent working order.\n\nDOCUMENTS:\nThe car comes with an ASI (Automotoclub Storico Italiano) registration certificate.",
